    <item>
      <title>Gwendolyn S. and Colby I. King Endowed Chair in Public Policy – The Cost of Opportunity: Reimagining College Affordability and Access at Founders Library</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54417572733766/huge/c16d07a228ec11516f9e028d39528c7096e60837.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 10 Nov 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>As the cost of higher education continues to shape the decisions and opportunities available to students and families, this important conversation will explore college affordability, federal education policy, financial aid, and the evolving value of a college degree.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>The discussion will also examine the critical role of Historically Black Colleges and Universities (HBCUs) in expanding educational access, advancing economic mobility, and preparing the next generation of leaders.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>The Honorable Nicholas Kent
<br>Under Secretary of Education
<br>U.S. Department of Education   </p>

<p>Moderated by Wayne A. I. Frederick, M.D., MBA
<br>President Emeritus
<br>Charles R. Drew Professor of Surgery
<br>Howard University   </p>

<p> </p>

<p>Tuesday, November 10, 2026
<br>11:00 a.m.
<br>Founders Library
<br>Howard University
<br>Washington, D.C.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Kindly RSVP by Friday 11/6/2026  </p>

<p> </p>

<p>Please confirm your attendance by RSVPing here: King/Colby Fireside Chat.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>We hope you will join us for this engaging exchange of ideas on one of the most pressing issues facing higher education today.</p>

<p><a href="https://events.howard.edu/event/kingcolby-lecture-series-ireside-conversation-the-cost-of-opportunity-reimagining-college-affordability-and-access">View on site</a> | <a href="mailto:?subject=I found an interesting event%3A Gwendolyn S. and Colby I. King Endowed Chair in Public Policy %E2%80%93 The Cost of Opportunity%3A Reimagining College Affordability and Access&amp;body=I found an interesting event you may like%3A%0A%0A%0ADate%3A Nov 10%2C 2026%0A%0ADescription%3A%0AAs the cost of higher education continues to shape the decisions and opportunities available to students and families%2C this important conversation will explore college affordability%2C federal education policy%2C financial aid%2C and the evolving value of a college degree.%0A%0A %0A%0AThe discussion will also examine the critical role of Historically Black Colleges and Universities %28HBCUs%29 in expanding educational access%2C advancing economic mobility%2C and preparing the next generation of leaders.%0A%0A %0A%0AThe Honorable Nicholas Kent%0AUnder Secretary of Education%0AU.S. Department of Education   %0A%0AModerated by Wayne A. I. Frederick%2C M.D.%2C MBA%0APresident Emeritus%0ACharles R. Drew Professor of Surgery%0AHoward University   %0A%0A %0A%0ATuesday%2C November 10%2C 2026%0A11%3A00 a.m.%0AFounders Library%0AHoward University%0AWashington%2C D.C.%0A%0A %0A%0AKindly RSVP by Friday 11%2F6%2F2026  %0A%0A %0A%0APlease confirm your attendance by RSVPing here%3A King%2FColby Fireside Chat.%0A%0A %0A%0AWe hope you will join us for this engaging exchange of ideas on one of the most pressing issues facing higher education today.%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fevents.howard.edu%2Fevent%2Fkingcolby-lecture-series-ireside-conversation-the-cost-of-opportunity-reimagining-college-affordability-and-access%0A">Email this event</a></p></div></div>]]></description>
